{"id":"b32","n":32,"title_ko":"Jamais Vu","title_en":"Jamais Vu","album":"Map of the Soul: Persona","year":2019,"yt":"G3x17KyNJtg","hook":[16,17,18,19,20,21,22],"notes":{"s":"A failure replayed so often it stops feeling familiar.","t":"A subunit track for Jin, J-Hope and Jungkook on Map of the Soul: Persona, and the album's darkest three minutes. The conceit is a video game: a run lost, a screen flashing game over, the wish that you could load a save instead of living with it. Underneath it is the specific fear of a performer who has made the same mistake before and cannot get numb to it. The title is the inverse of deja vu and names a real sensation, the moment something you have done a thousand times turns alien, and the Korean lyric uses the clinical Korean term for it outright.","k":[["내 미시감에 무서워지고","미시감 is the standard Korean term for jamais vu, built as not-yet-seen-feeling against 기시감, already-seen-feeling, for deja vu. The English title is a translation of a word the Korean lyric says plainly, so Korean listeners get the thesis of the song and English listeners get a French loan they have to look up."],["또 load하면 되겠지만","-(으)면 되다 means it's enough to do that, the pattern behind I could just reload. Pair it with -(으)면 안 되다, must not, and you have two of the most used constructions in spoken Korean."],["괜찮지만 괜찮지 않아","The same word contrasted against itself with -지만. Korean does this far more readily than English, and it marks a feeling the speaker refuses to resolve rather than a contradiction he has missed."],["시행착오와 오만 가지","오만 is fifty thousand, used as a vague huge number the way English says a million. Korean exaggeration counts in tens of thousands, so 오만 가지 is roughly a million different things."]]},"vocab":[{"w":"지다","en":"to lose, to be defeated","note":"Also to carry on your back and, of the sun, to set; three unrelated verbs spelled alike","i":0},{"w":"아른대다","en":"to flicker, to hover faintly in sight","note":"Used for things half-seen or half-remembered","i":2},{"w":"차라리","en":"rather, if anything I'd prefer","note":"Marks the lesser of two bad options","i":8},{"w":"완벽하다","en":"to be perfect, flawless","i":12},{"w":"탓하다","en":"to blame","note":"The noun 탓 is the fault itself; -는 탓에 means because of, always for a bad outcome","i":12},{"w":"멈추다","en":"to stop, to halt","i":17},{"w":"심장","en":"heart, the organ","note":"The feeling heart is 마음; 심장 is the one that beats","i":17},{"w":"뛰다","en":"to beat, to run, to leap","note":"One verb for a pulse, a sprint and a jump","i":17},{"w":"살리다","en":"to save, to bring back to life","note":"Causative of 살다, to live; 죽이다 is the opposite","i":19},{"w":"기회","en":"chance, opportunity","i":19},{"w":"끄다","en":"to turn off, to switch off","note":"Opposite 켜다; works for lights, devices and fires","i":24},{"w":"익숙하다","en":"to be used to, to be familiar with","i":26},{"w":"혼잣말","en":"talking to oneself, muttering","i":26},{"w":"부족하다","en":"to be lacking, not enough","note":"Also used of people, 실력이 부족하다, not good enough yet","i":28},{"w":"시행착오","en":"trial and error","note":"Four-character compound, written and slightly formal","i":29},{"w":"미시감","en":"jamais vu","note":"Mirrors 기시감, deja vu; both are everyday enough to appear in a pop lyric","i":31},{"w":"도망가다","en":"to run away, to flee","i":32},{"w":"그림자","en":"shadow","i":34},{"w":"넘어지다","en":"to fall over, to trip","note":"For a person going down; 떨어지다 is for things dropping","i":41},{"w":"반복되다","en":"to be repeated, to recur","note":"반복하다 is to repeat something; the -되다 form happens to you","i":42}],"items":[{"i":0,"ko":"또 져버린 것 같아","r":"tto jeobeorin geot kkata","tk":[{"s":"또","r":"tto","m":[{"t":"또","p":"MAG","pl":"adverb","en":["again, also"]}]},{"s":"져버린","r":"jeobeorin","m":[{"t":"져버린","p":"VV+EC+VX+ETM","pl":"verb"}]},{"s":"것","r":"geot","m":[{"t":"것","p":"NNB","pl":"counter / bound noun"}]},{"s":"같아","r":"gata","m":[{"t":"같","p":"VA","l":"같다","pl":"adjective","en":["to be like, to seem"]},{"t":"아","p":"EC","pl":"connect